{"id":"u-bf15b881-6ef2-499e-ae90-56b73eb694a3","src":"community","title":"Zoro Training program","author":"Inactive","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/gBJXlf-zoro-training-program","desc":"Inspired by the power, athletic resilience, and intensity of Zoro from One Piece, this program is built to help you develop aesthetic muscle physique, functional strength, explosive capability, and true mobility—all within a sustainable, long-term framework.\n\nThis is a complete physical development program designed to improve all aspects of your body.\n\nthis program strategically broken into 4 unique phases to challenge your body. \n\n🔹 Phase 1: Pure Hypertrophy (5 Weeks)\nThe foundation. A carefully designed 4-day split (Upper / Lower / Upper / Lower) focused on muscle with optimal volume and frequency. You’ll use a blend of compound lifts, isolation work, some bodyweight training, and strategic progression ranges to maximize growth without burnout.\n\nPrimary Goal: Muscle hypertrophy\nSecondary Focus: full body muscular hypotrophy, Stability, accessory development, movement quality\n\n🔹 Phase 2: Cardio & HIIT Week (1 Week)\nA high-intensity “reset” phase that is set to improce explosive athletic movement, fast-twitch fiber recruitment, and elite work capacity. You’ll hammer your conditioning, power, and mobility with sprint intervals, HIIT circuits, and deep yoga-style stretching.\n\nPrimary Goal: Athletic explosiveness + cardiovascular health\nSecondary Focus: flexibility\n\n🔹 Phase 3: Strength & Mobility (1 Week)\nA powerful mobility phase where you shift into unilateral lifts, mobility-driven, and core strength / Stability development. Think loaded carries, split squats, and Unilateral movements. \n\nPrimary Goal: Build strength, joint resilience, and control\nSecondary Focus: Movement quality, range of motion, injury-proofing\n\n🔹 Phase 4: Cardio & HIIT Week (Repeat)\nReturn to cardio, HIIT, and explosive training. This second run-through is meant to test what you’ve gained, shock the system again, and prepare you for another full cycle of growth.\n\nduring phase 1 and 3 make sure to add in a bit of low intensity cardio shoot for about 3 hours of cardio a week.","level":["Intermediate","Beginner"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":4,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-10-31T16:11:21.434Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Monday Upper","Tuesday Lower","Thursday Upper (push domninate","Friday lower","Cardio Hell week day 5 tabata","seeing the light!","out of hell"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Preacher Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Russian Twist (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"x":3}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":16,"x":3}],"note":"Make sure there is no chest support here"},{"n":"Shrug (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":16,"x":3}],"note":"really be slow 2 second positive, 2 second hold, 2 second negative."},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}],"note":"choose whatever lateral rase variation feels best for you"},{"n":"Overhead Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":3}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Front Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":7,"hi":10,"x":4}],"note":"focus on form. make sure to get your hips below your knee past parallel with  floor. try for full grip, if you can not the cross over grip works. the the elbows high! \n\npush with the quads glutes"},{"n":"Good Morning","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":18,"x":4}],"note":"go slow, fogous on the stretch. for the love of GOD don't go super heavy"}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Glute Bridge (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"x":3}],"note":"do theses on flat ground with a kettle bell on your waste. or not I'm not your Dad"},{"n":"Seated Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":20,"hi":25,"x":3}],"note":"if you can do theses with no pain standing do them standing. (more core activation)"}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Side Bend (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":3}],"note":"any oblique isolation will work like landmine oblique twist or windshield whippers but if its a body weight movement up the reps. (20-25)"},{"n":"Seated Row (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":3}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Kroc Row","sets":[{"lo":9,"hi":12,"x":3}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Decline Sit Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":17,"hi":20,"x":3}],"note":"add a twist at the top. really smoke that core ( double the reps per side)"},{"n":"Neck Curl","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"x":3}]},{"n":"Neck Extension","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"x":3}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Skull Crusher (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":3}],"note":"French press is good sub if you prefer it."},{"n":"Chest Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}],"note":"use a different variation from the one used Monday ( unless you only have dumbbells then keep at it *thumbs up*)"}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Reverse Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":3}],"note":"Hammer curl is a good sub"}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Hip Adductor (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hip Abductor (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"x":3}]},{"n":"Back Extension (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":16,"x":3}],"note":"Go light and keep the weight forward. The point is for the lower back isometric primarily"}]}]},null,null,null],[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Preacher Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Russian Twist (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"x":3}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":16,"x":3}]},{"n":"Shrug (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":16,"x":3}